\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. They who tread the path of
\par Labour follow where My feet have trod;
\par They who work without complaining
\par Do the holy will of God;
\par Nevermore thou needest seek Me;
\par I am with thee everywhere;
\par Raise the stone, and thou shalt find Me;
\par Cleave the wood and I am there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Where the many toil together,
\par There am I among my own;
\par Where the tired workman sleepeth,
\par There am I with him alone.
\par I, the Peace that passeth knowledge,
\par Dwell amid the daily strife;
\par I, the Bread of heaven, am broken
\par In the sacrament of life.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Every task, however simple, sets 
\par The soul that does it free;
\par Every deed of love and mercy
\par Done to man, it done to Me.
\par Nevermore thou needest seek Me;
\par I am with thee everywhere;
\par Raise the stone, and thou shalt find
\par Me; cleave the wood and I am there.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

